/*  A dispatcher: one clerk, two pipes, and whichever has something is served first.

    Customers send orders through one channel and complaints cancel tickets through another, each
    from a task of its own. The clerk does not know which will speak next, so it waits on BOTH at
    once with an automatic rabbit: each of its tasks names the channel it waits on, and at the
    rabbit's `Done.` the one whose delivery was SENT FIRST runs. The loop around it keeps serving.

    ★ The chosen task runs as the clerk's own code, so it can change the counts and the two
    `-open` facts directly. That is what lets the loop stop offering a channel once it has heard it
    close: a closed, empty channel runs its task with void, and stays ready on every later round.

    ★ Only the totals are printed. Compiled, the tasks are real threads, so orders and cancels may
    interleave differently on every run; the totals come out the same however they arrive.
*/

Pull a rabbit as hopper.
    Define orders as a channel of text.
    Define cancels as a channel of number.

    // Customers send their orders, then close the pipe.
    Have hopper start a task:
        For each vegetable in a series with ("kale", "carrots", "leeks"), repeat:
            Send vegetable through orders.
        Done.
        Close orders.
    Done.

    // Two tickets are cancelled.
    Have hopper start a task:
        Send 17 through cancels.
        Send 18 through cancels.
        Close cancels.
    Done.

    Define orders-open as true.
    Define cancels-open as true.
    Define packed as 0.
    Define cancelled as 0.
    While orders-open or cancels-open, repeat:
        Pull an automatic rabbit as grace.
            If orders-open:
                Have grace start a task for an order in orders:
                    If order is void:
                        The orders-open becomes false.
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        Increment packed by 1.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            If cancels-open:
                Have grace start a task for a ticket in cancels:
                    If ticket is void:
                        The cancels-open becomes false.
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        Increment cancelled by 1.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.
    State "packed {packed} orders, cancelled {cancelled} tickets".
Done.
